(vector (map (:adr/lesson-applied-proactively-7310 "tested via :risk/screen directly from the start (not via an actuation op against an unscreened campaign), applying parksafety's ADR-2607071922 Decision 5 / eldercare's, museum's, conservation's, salon's, entertainment's, casework's, hospital's, facility's, school's, association's, leasing's, behavioral's, secondary's, card's, water's, telecom's, aerospace's, recovery's, consulting's, union's, congregation's, fab's, energy's, care's, navigator's, learning's and banking's ADR-0001 lesson PROACTIVELY for a twenty-eighth consecutive vertical"), (:adr/misleading-claim-screen-design-7310 "misleading-claim-risk-unresolved-violations reuses the unconditional-evaluation discipline (casualty.governor/sanctions-violations's original fix) for a THIRTY-EIGHTH distinct grounding overall in this fleet, and is grep-verified as a GENUINELY NEW concept -- the only prior hit for 'misleading' (formation.governor) was read directly and confirmed to be an unrelated docstring mention about a misleading AUDIT-TRAIL record, not a misleading-advertising-claim concept -- grounded directly in this blueprint's own Trust Control 'a fabricated media-buy or misleading-claim risk forces a hold, not an override'"), (:adr/single-actuation-7310 "unlike most recent siblings, this blueprint's own README/business-model.md/operator-guide.md text names only ONE real-world act (placing/publishing a campaign on the client's behalf), so this build uses the single-actuation shape (#{:actuation/place-campaign}) matching leasing/underwriting/testlab/clinic/veterinary/funeral/parksafety/salon/entertainment/facility/consulting, rather than forcing a second actuation not grounded in the blueprint's own text"), (:adr/related (vector "2607071250-cloud-itonami-brokerage-6612-coverage" "2607071320-cloud-itonami-credit-6492-coverage" "2607071351-cloud-itonami-accounting-6920-coverage" "2607071618-cloud-itonami-marketadmin-6611-coverage" "2607071640-cloud-itonami-testlab-7120-coverage" "2607071654-cloud-itonami-clinic-8620-coverage" "2607071717-cloud-itonami-registrar-8530-coverage" "2607071732-cloud-itonami-wagering-9200-coverage" "2607071752-cloud-itonami-veterinary-7500-coverage" "2607071819-cloud-itonami-funeral-9603-coverage" "2607071849-cloud-itonami-repairshop-9521-coverage" "2607071922-cloud-itonami-parksafety-9321-coverage" "2607072715-cloud-itonami-eldercare-8730-coverage" "2607072730-cloud-itonami-museum-9102-coverage" "2607072745-cloud-itonami-conservation-9103-coverage" "2607072800-cloud-itonami-salon-9602-coverage" "2607072815-cloud-itonami-entertainment-9000-coverage" "2607072830-cloud-itonami-casework-8890-coverage" "2607072845-cloud-itonami-hospital-8610-coverage" "2607072900-cloud-itonami-facility-9311-coverage" "2607072915-cloud-itonami-school-8510-coverage" "2607080100-cloud-itonami-association-9412-coverage" "2607080200-cloud-itonami-leasing-6491-coverage" "2607080300-cloud-itonami-behavioral-8720-coverage" "2607080400-cloud-itonami-secondary-8521-coverage" "2607080500-cloud-itonami-card-6619-coverage" "2607080600-cloud-itonami-water-3600-coverage" "2607080700-cloud-itonami-telecom-6190-coverage" "2607080800-cloud-itonami-aerospace-3030-coverage" "2607080900-cloud-itonami-recovery-3830-coverage" "2607081000-cloud-itonami-consulting-7020-coverage" "2607081100-cloud-itonami-union-9420-coverage" "2607081200-cloud-itonami-congregation-9491-coverage" "2607081300-cloud-itonami-fab-2610-coverage" "2607081400-cloud-itonami-energy-3512-coverage" "2607081500-cloud-itonami-care-8810-coverage" "2607081600-cloud-itonami-navigator-8691-coverage" "2607081700-cloud-itonami-learning-8569-coverage" "2607081800-cloud-itonami-banking-6419-coverage" "2607032000-cloud-itonami-insurance-real-estate-coverage" "cloud-itonami-isic-6511/6512/6621/6622/6629/6520/6530/6820/6612/6492/6920/6611/7120/8620/8530/9200/7500/9603/9521/9321/8730/9102/9103/9602/9000/8890/8610/9311/8510/9412/6491/8720/8521/6619/3600/6190/3030/3830/7020/9420/9491/2610/3512/8810/8691/8569/6419 ADR-0001s" "langgraph-clj ADR-0001")), (:adr/status :accepted), (:adr/id "2607081900"), (:adr/blueprint-already-correct-7310 "unlike most prior promotions this window, this repo's blueprint.edn already had the correct isic- prefixed :id and correctly populated :required-technologies/:optional-technologies matching the kotoba-lang/industry registry's own entry for \"7310\" exactly -- only the :maturity field itself needed adding, confirmed by reading blueprint.edn before editing rather than assuming a fix was needed"), (:adr/fleet-maturity-before "{:implemented 53, :blueprint 31, :spec 546, :total 643}"), (:adr/next-vertical-selection-unconstrained true), (:adr/doc_type "adr"), (:adr/body "# ADR-2607081900: `cloud-itonami-isic-7310` (advertising) deepened to `:implemented`\n\n## Status\n\nAccepted.\n\n## Related\n\n- ADR-2607032000 (original insurance/real-estate batch)\n- ADR-2607081600 (`cloud-itonami-isic-8691`, health access navigation)\n- ADR-2607081700 (`cloud-itonami-isic-8569`, community learning support)\n- ADR-2607081800 (`cloud-itonami-isic-6419`, community monetary intermediation)\n- `cloud-itonami-isic-7310/docs/adr/0001-architecture.md` (child-repo architecture ADR)\n- `langgraph-clj` ADR-0001 (StateGraph actor pattern)\n\n## Context\n\n`cloud-itonami-isic-7310` publishes an OSS business blueprint for\nadvertising: creating and placing advertising campaigns for clients\nacross media. Like every prior vertical in this fleet, the blueprint\ntext alone is not an implementation — this ADR records the governed-\nactor build that promotes `cloud-itonami-isic-7310` from `:blueprint`\nto `:implemented` in the `kotoba-lang/industry` registry, the\nfortieth vertical built outside ADR-2607032000's original insurance/\nreal-estate batch.\n\n## Problem\n\n1. `cloud-itonami-isic-7310`'s blueprint described a real-world\n   advertising-agency operating model (campaign intake, media-plan\n   assessment, misleading-claim-risk screening, campaign placement)\n   but had no governed-actor implementation: no Store, no Governor, no\n   rollout phasing, no tests.\n2. Unlike most recent siblings, the blueprint's own README,\n   business-model.md and operator-guide.md consistently name only ONE\n   real-world act (\"placing/publishing a campaign on the client's\n   behalf\") — this build needed to decide whether to honor that\n   single-actuation shape or force a second actuation not grounded in\n   the text.\n3. The blueprint's own Trust Controls name a concrete hold condition\n   not seen under this exact name in any prior sibling: \"a fabricated\n   media-buy or misleading-claim risk forces a hold, not an override.\"\n\n## Decision\n\n1. **Single-actuation shape.** Matching `leasing`/`underwriting`/\n   `testlab`/`clinic`/`veterinary`/`funeral`/`parksafety`/`salon`/\n   `entertainment`/`facility`/`consulting`'s single-actuation shape,\n   `high-stakes` is the one-member set `#{:actuation/place-campaign}`.\n2. **Entity and op shape.** Primary entity `campaign`. Four ops:\n   `:campaign/intake`, `:media-plan/verify`, `:risk/screen`, and\n   `:actuation/place-campaign` (high-stakes).\n3. **`media-spend-exceeds-authorized-budget?` — 7th MAXIMUM-ceiling\n   check.** Following `facility`, `school`, `card`, `recovery`,\n   `care` and `navigator`, this applies the same ceiling-only\n   comparison to a campaign's proposed media spend against its own\n   recorded authorized budget, gating only `:actuation/place-\n   campaign`.\n4. **`misleading-claim-risk-unresolved-violations` — 38th\n   unconditional-evaluation screening grounding, a genuinely new\n   concept.** Every prior sibling's `governor.cljc` was grepped for\n   \"misleading\" before this claim was finalized — one hit\n   (`formation.governor`), read directly and confirmed to be an\n   unrelated docstring mention about a misleading audit-trail record,\n   not a misleading-advertising-claim concept. Grounded directly in\n   the blueprint's own Trust Control text. Gates both `:risk/screen`\n   and `:actuation/place-campaign`.\n5. **Dedicated double-actuation-guard boolean.** `:campaign-placed?`\n   on the `campaign` record, never a single `:status` value.\n6. **Store protocol, MemStore + DatomicStore parity**, proven via\n   `test/advertising/store_contract_test.clj`. The per-entity accessor\n   is safely named `campaign` directly.\n7. **Phase 0→3 rollout** — Phase 3 `:auto` set is `{:campaign/intake}`\n   only; the actuation is permanently excluded from every phase's\n   `:auto` set.\n8. **No bespoke domain capability lib** — runs on the generic\n   robotics/identity/forms/dmn/bpmn/audit-ledger stack.\n9. **Mock + LLM advisor pair** — `mock-advisor` default everywhere,\n   `llm-advisor` with a defensive EDN-proposal parser.\n10. **No `blueprint.edn` field-sync fixes needed this time.** Unlike\n    most prior promotions this window, this repo's `blueprint.edn`\n    already had the correct `isic-` prefixed `:id` and correctly\n    populated `:required-technologies`/`:optional-technologies`\n    matching the `kotoba-lang/industry` registry's own entry exactly —\n    confirmed by reading `blueprint.edn` before editing, rather than\n    assuming a fix was needed. Only the `:maturity` field itself\n    needed adding.\n\n## Consequences\n\n- Fifty-fourth actor in this fleet (53 implemented before this\n  build).\n- Confirms the MAXIMUM-ceiling check family generalizes to a\n  seventh, genuinely distinct domain (media-budget authorization).\n- Establishes a genuinely new unconditional-evaluation-screening\n  concept (misleading-claim-risk), grep-verified absent from every\n  prior sibling.\n- `MemStore` ‖ `DatomicStore` parity proven by contract test.\n- Fleet maturity: `:implemented` 53 → 54, `:blueprint` 31 → 30,\n  `:spec` 546 unchanged, total 643.\n- Test status: 30 tests / 127 assertions (leaner than dual-actuation\n  builds, matching the single-actuation shape), lint clean, demo\n  verified end-to-end.\n- Next vertical selection remains unconstrained under the standing\n  authorization.\n\n## Alternatives considered\n\n| Alternative | Rejected because |\n|---|---|\n| A dual-actuation shape (e.g. a separate \"publish creative asset\" actuation) | The blueprint's own text consistently names only ONE real-world act — inventing a second would not be grounded in the blueprint's own text |\n| A single \"campaign-safety\" check merging budget and misleading-claim concerns | Authorized-budget is a ground-truth numeric recompute; misleading-claim-risk status is an unconditionally-evaluated flag needing the screening op to self-hold — merging loses that property |\n\n## References\n\n- `orgs/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isic-7310/docs/adr/0001-architecture.md`\n- `orgs/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isic-7310/README.edn`\n- `orgs/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isic-7310/docs/business-model.md`\n- `orgs/kotoba-lang/industry/resources/kotoba/industry/registry.edn` (entry `\"7310\"`)"), (:adr/fleet-maturity-after "{:implemented 54, :blueprint 30, :spec 546, :total 643}"), (:adr/test-status-7310 "30 tests / 127 assertions (leaner than dual-actuation builds, matching the single-actuation shape), lint clean, demo verified end-to-end (one clean single-actuation lifecycle plus four HARD-hold cases)"), (:adr/date "2026-07-08"), (:adr/distinctive-check-7310 "media-spend-exceeds-authorized-budget? is the SEVENTH instance of this fleet's MAXIMUM-ceiling check family (facility/school/card/recovery/care/navigator established the first six), a direct, natural mapping onto real ad-agency media-buying practice, closely analogous to card's settlement-amount-exceeds-authorized? shape"), (:adr/scope-note "this is a NEW ADR because ISIC 7310 (advertising) has a genuinely distinct media-buying/misleading-claim concern from every prior professional-services sibling (consulting/7020, testlab/7120), warranting its own record per this fleet's standing per-vertical-ADR convention"), (:db/id -1), (:adr/deepened-to-implemented "cloud-itonami-isic-7310"), (:adr/pattern-7310 "sealed AdOps-LLM + independent Campaign Governor + append-only audit ledger, modeled closely on all fifty-three prior actors; FORTIETH build outside ADR-2607032000's original insurance/real-estate batch (after 6612, 6492, 6920, 6611, 7120, 8620, 8530, 9200, 7500, 9603, 9521, 9321, 8730, 9102, 9103, 9602, 9000, 8890, 8610, 9311, 8510, 9412, 6491, 8720, 8521, 6619, 3600, 6190, 3030, 3830, 7020, 9420, 9491, 2610, 3512, 8810, 8691, 8569, 6419)"), (:adr/title "cloud-itonami-isic-7310 (advertising) deepened to :implemented -- fortieth vertical outside the original batch"), (:adr/source-format "edn")))